L. Horn, _A Natural History of Negation_

It was the primary source in the revision of negation that was described in 
the "Negation Paper", now absorbed into various places in the Book.  pc 
read it thorough; I rather less so, since I didn't have the knowledge of 
linguistics to handle it at the time (this was 1989).

And no, I don't speak that dialect of English, which seems to have become 
commonplace in the US in the last decade or so.  It drives me batty to read 
sentences like that that seem to make universal claims, but don't really do so.

